CAT = "s66Ethics"; SEG = "ETH"
Q = [
('A research tool is used partly for research and partly for billing. Under Section 28(e), soft dollars may pay for:',
 'Only the research share', ['Its full cost', 'None of its cost', 'Its full cost with consent'],
 'Section 28(e) covers only brokerage and research services. For a mixed-use item, the manager must allocate a reasonable share to research and pay the rest with its own money.'),
('An SEC-registered adviser may generally charge a performance fee to:',
 'Qualified clients', ['Any client who agrees in writing', 'Clients over age 65', 'Retail clients only'],
 'Advisers Act Section 205 bars performance fees except as allowed by rule. SEC Rule 205-3 permits them for qualified clients, who meet asset or net worth tests.'),
('After a covered associate makes a disqualifying contribution to an official, the adviser cannot be paid by that government entity for:',
 'Two years', ['One year', 'Six months', 'Five years'],
 'SEC Rule 206(4)-5 imposes a two-year time-out on compensation for advising the government entity after a contribution above the de minimis amounts.'),
("Under the SEC's pay-to-play rule, a covered associate entitled to vote for the official may give, per election, without triggering a time-out:",
 'Up to $350', ['Up to $150', 'Up to $250', 'Up to $1,000'],
 'Rule 206(4)-5 allows $350 per election to an official the associate can vote for, and $150 to one the associate cannot vote for. $250 is the MSRB Rule G-37 figure for municipal dealers.'),
('An adviser has custody of client assets when it:',
 'Can deduct fees from client accounts', ["Advises on a client's held-away account", 'Gets duplicate statements', 'Recommends a custodian'],
 'Authority to withdraw funds, including deducting advisory fees directly, is custody under SEC Rule 206(4)-2. Receiving copies of statements or giving advice does not give access to the assets.'),
('An adviser that inadvertently receives client securities does not have custody if it returns them to the sender within:',
 'Three business days', ['Ten business days', '30 calendar days', '24 hours'],
 'SEC Rule 206(4)-2 excludes funds or securities received inadvertently and returned to the sender promptly, and in any case within three business days.'),
('Client assets held under the SEC custody rule are generally verified each year by:',
 'Surprise accountant exam', ['Scheduled SEC audit', 'Review by the client', 'Annual FINRA branch exam'],
 'An adviser with custody must generally arrange a yearly surprise examination by an independent public accountant, at a time the accountant picks without notice.'),
('A client tells an agent to buy 100 shares of a named stock today at the best price available. This order:',
 'Is not discretionary', ['Needs written discretion', 'Is prohibited', 'Gives the agent discretion over the asset'],
 'Choosing only the time or price for an order the client gave, naming the security, action and amount, is not discretion. Choosing the security, amount or action would be.'),
("An adviser may share a client's holdings with an outside party without consent when:",
 'Required by law or subpoena', ['Another client asks to see them', 'It would help firm marketing', "The client's friend asks"],
 "NASAA's unethical practices rule bars disclosing a client's identity, affairs or investments without consent unless required by law. Marketing and curiosity are never reasons."),
('Under the Uniform Prudent Investor Act, a trustee judges each investment:',
 'As part of the whole portfolio', ['On its merits alone', 'By its current yield only', 'Against a state legal list'],
 'The UPIA adopted a total portfolio approach based on Modern Portfolio Theory: no investment is imprudent on its own, and risk and return are judged for the portfolio as a whole.'),
('A broker-dealer must file a Suspicious Activity Report on a suspicious transaction involving at least:',
 '$5,000', ['$10,000', '$3,000', '$2,000'],
 'Bank Secrecy Act rules require broker-dealers to file a SAR for suspicious transactions of $5,000 or more. $10,000 is the threshold for currency transaction reports.'),
('After filing a Suspicious Activity Report, the firm may tell the customer:',
 'Nothing about the filing', ['About it within 30 days', 'About it only if asked', 'About it once the case closes'],
 'SAR filings are confidential, and disclosing a filing or its contents to the subject is prohibited. The firm may still decide to close the account.'),
('Moving illegal money through many accounts and transfers to hide where it came from is the money laundering stage called:',
 'Layering', ['Placement', 'Integration', 'Structuring'],
 'Placement puts cash into the financial system, layering disguises its trail, and integration returns it as apparently clean funds. Structuring is splitting cash deposits to avoid reporting.'),
("Under NASAA's unethical practices rule for investment advisers, an adviser may borrow from a client that is:",
 'Bank that makes loans', ['Longtime personal friend', 'Wealthy retired client', 'Fellow club member'],
 "NASAA's rule treats borrowing from a client as unethical unless the client is a broker-dealer, an affiliate of the adviser, or a financial institution engaged in lending."),
("An agent may share in the profits and losses of a customer's account only if:",
 'Firm and customer agree in writing', ['Customer alone agrees verbally', 'Only gains, never losses, are shared', 'Account is over five years old'],
 "Sharing requires prior written approval from the firm and the customer, and the share must generally match the agent's own contribution, except for immediate family accounts."),
('A client trades after her brother, a company director, tells her about an unannounced merger. This is:',
 'Illegal insider trading', ['Legal since she is not an employee', 'Front running', 'Market timing'],
 "Trading on material nonpublic information received from an insider who breached a duty is illegal for the tipper and the tippee. Front running means trading ahead of a customer's order."),
('An agent buys a stock for her own account just before entering a large customer buy order. This is:',
 'Front running', ['Selling away', 'Churning', 'Freeriding'],
 "Front running is trading ahead of a customer's order to profit from the expected price move, and it is a dishonest practice. Selling away is dealing outside the firm."),
("Under NASAA's model rule, an adviser that charges a fee clearly too high for the services provided is:",
 'Acting unethically', ['Within its rights if disclosed', 'Fine for wealthy clients', 'Regulated only by the SEC'],
 'Charging a client an unreasonable advisory fee is listed as an unethical business practice. Disclosure does not cure a fee that is unreasonable in light of the services.'),
('Under SEC Rule 204A-1, a new access person must submit a holdings report within:',
 '10 days', ['30 days', '45 days', '5 days'],
 'The initial holdings report is due within 10 days of becoming an access person, with information no more than 45 days old. Annual holdings reports follow each year.'),
('Under SEC Rule 204A-1, access persons submit transaction reports no later than how long after each calendar quarter ends?',
 '30 days', ['10 days', '45 days', '90 days'],
 'Quarterly transaction reports are due within 30 days after quarter end and cover all reportable trades in the quarter. Initial holdings reports are due within 10 days.'),
('A trusted contact person on a customer account is someone the firm may contact about:',
 'Possible exploitation', ['Approving new trades', 'Margin calls on the account', 'Changing the beneficiary'],
 "FINRA Rule 4512 asks firms to seek a trusted contact they may reach to address possible financial exploitation or confirm the customer's health or whereabouts. The contact has no authority over the account."),
("NASAA's model rule on business continuity and succession planning requires a state adviser's plan to address:",
 'Death or disability of key staff', ['Annual advisory fee increases', 'Client tax filing dates', 'Marketing plans during system outages'],
 'Model Rule 203(a)-1 requires written plans for business disruptions, including protecting records and client access, and for the death, incapacity or departure of key personnel.'),
('In an agency cross transaction, an adviser may not:',
 'Recommend it to both sides', ['Act as broker for both sides', 'Receive a commission', 'Get client consent in writing'],
 "An agency cross is allowed with the client's written consent, disclosure and confirmations, but the adviser cannot have recommended the trade to both the buyer and the seller."),
('After making a recommendation, Regulation Best Interest generally does not require a broker-dealer to:',
 'Monitor the account continuously', ['Disclose material conflicts', 'Have a reasonable basis for it', 'Keep records of it'],
 'Reg BI applies at the time of the recommendation, with disclosure, care, conflict and compliance obligations. It does not impose ongoing account monitoring unless the firm agrees to provide it.'),
]
